{%- comment -%}
  ============================================================
  ESSENTIAL PREORDER — DISCOUNT WIDGET · UNIFIED SNIPPET
  ============================================================
  Single snippet. Two visual designs. Zero JS duplication.

  Designs:  'native'    — light / Horizon-safe (default)
            'editorial' — dark / premium editorial

  Usage (inside a Custom Liquid block):
    {% render 'preorder-discount-widget', pw_design: 'native' %}
    {% render 'preorder-discount-widget', pw_design: 'editorial' %}

  Placement inside Theme Editor block order:
    ▸ Variant Picker
    ▸ ← INSERT Custom Liquid block here →
    ▸ Buy Buttons

  ----- INSTALL -----
  1. Save as: snippets/preorder-discount-widget.liquid
  2. In Theme Editor → Custom Liquid block, add ONE of:
       {% render 'preorder-discount-widget', pw_design: 'native' %}
       {% render 'preorder-discount-widget', pw_design: 'editorial' %}
  3. App Embeds → Essential Preorder & Back in Stock → ON
  4. Set a discount in the app (Content → Discount)

  ----- PER-MERCHANT TOKENS -----
  Native:    --pdw-active-border, --pdw-save-bg, --pdw-radius, --pdw-font
  Editorial: --pdw-accent, --pdw-active-bg, --pdw-radius, --pdw-display-font

  ----- ARCHITECTURE NOTES -----
  • Liquid controls ONLY which CSS modifier class renders.
  • Widget visibility is driven by [data-pdw-state] attribute — NO inline
    style writes. CSS .essential-pdw { display:none } /
    .essential-pdw[data-pdw-state="active"] { display:block } ensures
    the widget is never visible before JS hydrates it, and eliminates
    the style-attribute MutationObserver feedback loop present in v1.

  JS LIFECYCLE (ported from design1 — QA-passed pattern)
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  • window.__pwModule guard is an OBJECT { reinit } not a boolean.
    Subsequent script executions after Horizon section re-renders call
    reinit() directly instead of bailing out.
  • teardown() disconnects all observers and nulls every cached ref
    before each reinit(). Prevents stale observers from firing into
    detached nodes alongside fresh ones.
  • buildCache() caches all DOM targets once per init cycle.
  • Observers are SCOPED:
      - observers.payment → payment button container (class attr only)
      - observers.prices  → prices-block subtree (text / class changes)
      - observers.fallback → document.body, self-destructs once targets found
    No broad document.body observer watching style changes — eliminates
    the write→observe→write feedback loop that caused blinking in v1.
  • evaluateVariant() = isPreorderVariant() && hasDiscount() → show/hide.
    Reads prices from [data-essential-preorder-element="regular"] and
    [data-essential-preorder-element="compare-at"] directly — no
    brittle span/money heuristics.
  • All DOM writes happen synchronously inside evaluateVariant().
    The 32 ms debounce on the observer callback is sufficient batching;
    no rAF needed, which eliminates the __pdwPending guard complexity.
  • shopify:section:load → reinit()  (Section Rendering API)
  • page:loaded         → reinit()  (Horizon soft-nav completion)
  • variant:changed     → debouncedEvaluate (product form event)
  ============================================================
{%- endcomment -%}

